From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] J604 local build: name the whole Apple F-row in Super+K,
 leave out absent keys

key-names named only the brightness keys (F1/F2), so the Super+K list on a
MacBook still ended in raw keysym rows: XF86AudioRaiseVolume,
XF86AudioMute, ... for keys printed F5 and F7-F12, XF86PowerOff for the
Touch ID key, and XF86KbdBrightnessUp/Down, XF86KbdLightOnOff,
XF86AudioPause, XF86Eject, XF86Calculator and XF86Touchpad* for keys an
Apple keyboard does not have.

The built-in keyboard and the 2021/2024 Magic Keyboards share one fn table
in hid-apple (magic_keyboard_2021_and_2024_fn_keys): F1/F2 brightness, F3
KEY_SCALE, F4 KEY_SEARCH, F5 KEY_MICMUTE, F6 KEY_SLEEP, F7-F9
previous/play-pause/next, F10-F12 mute/volume down/up; no keyboard-backlight,
eject or separate pause key. Through xkeyboard-config's evdev keycodes those
are XF86AudioMicMute, XF86AudioPrev, XF86AudioPlay, XF86AudioNext,
XF86AudioMute, XF86AudioLowerVolume and XF86AudioRaiseVolume, named here
F5 and F7-F12 as the brightness keys already are; macsmc-input's power
key is KEY_POWER, XF86PowerOff, named POWER. The keys Omarchy binds that
the keyboard lacks are named "-", which omarchy's menu (4.5.0-3.3 J604
build) reads as "leave the rows out"; an older menu ignores those lines.
The bindings themselves are not changed, and Ctrl + F1/F2 stay the
keyboard backlight keys.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 omarchy-mac/README.md                         |  2 +-
 omarchy-mac/share/omarchy-platform/key-names  | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 test/integration/apple-platform-hooks-test.sh |  9 +++++++--
 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/omarchy-mac/README.md b/omarchy-mac/README.md
index 00564f1..49f187e 100644
--- a/omarchy-mac/README.md
+++ b/omarchy-mac/README.md
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ System setup also wraps Chromium, 1Password and Cursor where they are installed:
 
 The Mac's hardware data lives in the platform root, `/usr/share/omarchy-platform`, which Omarchy reads at that fixed path and ships nothing in, so Omarchy's own config carries no Apple branch. All of it is data. The package ships no Hyprland files and changes no Hyprland binds or settings: Omarchy's binds, trackpad and cursor defaults apply on a Mac as on any other machine. A key the built-in keyboard lacks is given to it below Hyprland, as a udev hwdb remap in this package (omacom/omarchy-mac-pkgs#6, in review).
 
-- `key-names`: the keybindings menu shows `XF86MonBrightnessUp` and `Down` as the F2 and F1 they are.
+- `key-names`: the keybindings menu shows each key an Apple keyboard sends as the key printed on it: `XF86MonBrightnessUp` and `Down` as F2 and F1, the microphone, media and volume keys as F5 and F7 to F12, `XF86PowerOff` as POWER (the Touch ID key). Keys Omarchy binds that an Apple keyboard does not have (keyboard backlight, separate pause, eject, calculator, touchpad toggles) are named `-`, so the menu leaves their rows out; Ctrl + F1/F2 are the keyboard backlight keys. The bindings stay.
 - `display-cutouts.json`: the notch of each MacBook panel (the 14" Pro measured at 64 physical rows, the 16" Pro inferred at 64 and the Airs at 56), which the bar keeps clear of. A notched panel not listed gets no floor until the file lists it; `[bar] notch-height` in `shell.toml` only adjusts the floor of a listed panel.
 - `displays.conf`: `omarchy-hw-display` never picks the Touch Bar's `display-pipe` or `228600000.dsi.0` backlight and prefers the Retina panel's `apple-panel-bl` (no GPU backlight exists), and `omarchy-brightness-display` probes an external monitor over DDC only when its connector has a `ddc` node, since Apple's display driver registers no DDC channel and a probe would walk the SoC's SMBus for about 3 s.
 - `idle.json`: the keyboard backlight goes off after 10 seconds without keyboard or trackpad input and comes back at its level on the next input, as on macOS (the runtime's `idle.keyboardBacklight`, which a user's `shell.json` overrides; `0` turns it off). A runtime older than the setting ignores it.
diff --git a/omarchy-mac/share/omarchy-platform/key-names b/omarchy-mac/share/omarchy-platform/key-names
index 58264ee..8872ee7 100644
--- a/omarchy-mac/share/omarchy-platform/key-names
+++ b/omarchy-mac/share/omarchy-platform/key-names
@@ -1,2 +1,19 @@
 XF86MonBrightnessUp F2
 XF86MonBrightnessDown F1
+XF86AudioMicMute F5
+XF86AudioPrev F7
+XF86AudioPlay F8
+XF86AudioNext F9
+XF86AudioMute F10
+XF86AudioLowerVolume F11
+XF86AudioRaiseVolume F12
+XF86PowerOff POWER
+XF86KbdBrightnessUp -
+XF86KbdBrightnessDown -
+XF86KbdLightOnOff -
+XF86AudioPause -
+XF86Eject -
+XF86Calculator -
+XF86TouchpadToggle -
+XF86TouchpadOn -
+XF86TouchpadOff -
diff --git a/test/integration/apple-platform-hooks-test.sh b/test/integration/apple-platform-hooks-test.sh
index 74f1267..5f1e6e0 100644
--- a/test/integration/apple-platform-hooks-test.sh
+++ b/test/integration/apple-platform-hooks-test.sh
@@ -22,9 +22,14 @@ done
 
 [[ ! -e $platform_root/hypr ]] || fail "omarchy-mac ships no Hyprland files; Omarchy's own config carries the Mac's binds"
 
-# The keybindings menu shows the brightness keys as the F1 and F2 they are.
-[[ $(<"$platform_root/key-names") == $'XF86MonBrightnessUp F2\nXF86MonBrightnessDown F1' ]] ||
+# The keybindings menu shows the brightness keys as the F1 and F2 they are,
+# the rest of the F-row the same way, and leaves out keys a Mac keyboard lacks.
+grep -Fxq 'XF86MonBrightnessUp F2' "$platform_root/key-names" && grep -Fxq 'XF86MonBrightnessDown F1' "$platform_root/key-names" ||
   fail "omarchy-mac names the brightness keys F2 and F1"
+grep -Fxq 'XF86AudioRaiseVolume F12' "$platform_root/key-names" && grep -Fxq 'XF86KbdBrightnessUp -' "$platform_root/key-names" ||
+  fail "omarchy-mac names the volume keys and leaves the absent keyboard-backlight keys out"
+! grep -Evq '^XF86[A-Za-z0-9_]+ ([A-Z0-9]+|-)$' "$platform_root/key-names" ||
+  fail "every key-names line is a keysym and an upper-case key name or -"
 grep -Fq /usr/share/omarchy-platform/key-names "$runtime/bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings" || fail "the keybindings menu reads the platform's key names"
 pass "the keybindings menu names the Mac's brightness keys as its F-keys"
 
